# Key Insights

## 1. Strong Balance-Sheet Expansion

Total Assets increased by 202.1% between FY2020 and FY2024, indicating substantial expansion in the bank's overall balance sheet.

## 2. Strong Lending Growth

Customer Loans increased by 191.0% over the same period, demonstrating significant expansion of the lending portfolio.

## 3. Funding Growth

Customer Deposits increased by 175.5%, providing substantial growth in the customer funding base.

## 4. Profitability Improvement

Profit After Tax increased by 152.5% between FY2020 and FY2024, indicating significant improvement in absolute profitability.

## 5. Improving Credit Risk

Gross NPL Ratio declined from 5.5% in FY2020 to 4.1% in FY2024, representing a 1.4 percentage-point improvement.

## 6. Strengthening Provision Coverage

Loan Loss Coverage increased from 0.47x in FY2020 to 1.19x in FY2024, indicating stronger coverage against credit risk.

## 7. Funding Risk to Monitor

Customer Loans grew by 191.0%, compared with 175.5% growth in Customer Deposits. This indicates that lending growth outpaced deposit growth and warrants continued monitoring of sustainable funding.

## Management Implication

UAB Bank has achieved substantial growth while profitability and key risk indicators improved. The main strategic consideration is maintaining sustainable funding, asset quality and cost discipline as the bank continues to expand.